{{also|Urban}}
==English==

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*gʰerdʰ-|*werbʰ-|*-nós}}
Borrowed from {{bor|en|frm|urbain|t=belonging to a city, urban; courteous, refined, urbane}} (modern {{cog|fr|urbain}}), or from its {{glossary|etymon}} {{der|en|la|urbānus|t=of or belonging to a city, urban; of manners or style: like those of city dwellers: cultivated, polished, refined, sophisticated}} + [[w:English language|English]] {{m|en|-an|pos={{glossary|suffix}} meaning ‘of or pertaining to’ forming {{glossary|adjective}}s}}. {{m|la||Urbānus}} is derived from {{m|la|urbs|t=city; walled town; Rome}} (further etymology uncertain, possibly from {{der|en|ine-pro|*gʰerdʰ-|t=to encircle, enclose; a belt; an enclosure, fence}} or {{m|ine-pro|*werbʰ-|t=to enclose}}) + {{m|la|-ānus|pos=suffix meaning ‘of or pertaining to’ forming adjectives}}.

