===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Of, pertaining to, [[characteristic#Adjective|characteristic]] of, or [[happen#Verb|happening]] or [[locate]]d in, a [[city]] or [[town]]; of, pertaining to, or characteristic of [[life#Noun|life]] in such a [[place#Noun|place]], especially when [[contrast#Verb|contrasted]] with the [[countryside]].
#: {{coi|en|'''urban''' life&emsp;&emsp;&emsp; '''urban''' traffic}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Audrey Garric|title=Urban canopies let nature bloom|magazine=w:The Guardian Weekly|url=http://www.guardian.co.uk/environment/2013/may/04/paris-green-roofs-building-climate-environment|date=2013-05-10|volume=188|issue=22|page=30|passage=As towns continue to grow, replanting vegetation has become a form of '''urban''' utopia and green roofs are spreading fast. Last year 1m square metres of plant-covered roofing was built in France, as much as in the US, and 10 times more than in Germany, the pioneer in this field. In Paris 22 hectares of roof have been planted, out of a potential total of 80 hectares.}}
# [[live#Verb|Living]] in a city or town.
#* {{RQ:Pliny Holland Historie of the World|tome=1|book=XVIII|chapter=Of Iugerum, and Actus. Of the Ancient Lawes Ordained for Cattell in Old Time. How Often and at what Times Corn and Victuals were Exceeding Cheape at Rome. What Noble and Famous Persons Addicted Themselves Wholly to Husbandrie and Tillage.|pages=550–551|pageref=551|passage=Inſomuch, as thoſe citizens vvere reputed for cheeſe and principall, vvho vvere poſſeſſed of land and living in the countrey: and theſe made the State, called the Ruſtick Tribes, in Rome: vvheras contrarivviſe the other eſtate, reputed the meaner in degree, vvas named the '''Vrbane''' Tribes; conſiſting of Artiſanes & ſuch like as vvere not landed perſons: into vvhich, if a man vvere transferred from any of the reſt, it vvas thought a great ſhame and diſgrace, as if hee vvere reproched for idleneſſe and negligence in husbandrie.}}
#* {{RQ:Topsell Foure-footed Beastes|chapter=Of the Vulgar Little Mouse|page=504|passage=The Epithets of myce are thes; ſhort, ſmall, fearful, peaceable, ridiculous, ruſtik, or country mouſe, '''vrbane''', or citty mouſe, {{...}}}}
# [[have#Verb|Having]] [[authority]] or [[jurisdiction]] over a city or town.
#* {{RQ:Howell SPQV|chapter=Of Officers or Magistrats in Generall|page=16|passage=All theſe Magiſtrats are but temporary, and have a time limited them; the '''Urbane''' or Citty Magiſtrats ſome of them continue in office 6. months, others 8. months, others are annuall; {{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|US|proscribed|outdated}} Relating to [[contemporary]] [[African American]] [[culture]], especially in music.
# {{lb|en|US|UK|euphemism|offensive}} (of inhabitants or residents) Black; African American.

====Usage notes====
* The word "urban" in a musical context came to be controversial and it was described as perpetuating and reinforcing the racial stereotyping of black communities, especially black musicians,<ref>{{cite-journal|date=14 August 2018|author=Kehinde Andrews|title='Urban' sounds: it's time to stop using this hackneyed term for black music|journal=The Guardian|url=https://www.theguardian.com/music/shortcuts/2018/aug/14/urban-time-stop-hackneyed-term-black-music|passage=Industry executives are increasingly railing against the word, which is born out of racial stereotyping of black communities.}}</ref> and as a "catchall for music created by Black artists, regardless of genre", leading to the music industry's replacement of it with more appropriate terms.<ref>{{cite-journal|author=Sophie Lewis|url=https://www.cbsnews.com/news/grammy-awards-rename-controversial-urban-category/|title=Grammy Awards renames controversial "urban" category|journal=CBS News|date=11 June 2020|passage=The Grammys has announced that it is dropping the term "urban" from its awards show following criticism from black artists.}}</ref>
* "Urban" as a descriptor of black inhabitants or residents is an offensive and stereotypical usage; see Dictionary.com's "Historical usage of urban" for the explanation.<ref>{{cite-book|year=2012|url=https://www.dictionary.com/browse/urban|title=Urban|publisher=Dictionary.com|passage=5 ''Offensive''. (used as a euphemism for Black or African American, rather than in reference to cities or their residents)}}</ref>

